    "narrative": "For our July 4th slate, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Tyler Freeman** (72.83) emerge as our top-tier plays, both capitalizing on high-ceiling matchups against starters with shaky xERAs (4.48 and 4.76, respectively). **Lawrence Butler** benefits immensely from a favorable park factor and a top-of-the-order boost, while **Tyler Freeman** gains significant value from a pitcher-park mismatch that should allow his offensive upside to shine. Meanwhile, **Luis Arraez** (69.53) remains a high-floor start against the struggling Sullivan; despite the platoon disadvantage, the combination of a generous park factor and a spot in the two-hole makes him a primary anchor for our AVG category today.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Taylor Ward** (41.87). While **Taylor Ward** offers solid output, he was ultimately edged out due to the stiff matchup against Greene, whose lower xERA (3.06) suppressed the score below the threshold required to crack our starting rotation. We are navigating significant roster constraints with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Matt Chapman** all sidelined on the IL, placing additional pressure on our secondary options like **Gavin Sheets** (46.35) and **Daulton Varsho** (47.69). While these two remain in the lineup today, their marginal scores are a direct result of facing elite arms like Yamamoto and Gilbert.\n\nManagers should remain vigilant regarding the risk profile of **Cal Raleigh** (64.17). While he maintains a solid score, he faces Bieber\u2014a high-skill arm that could mitigate his power potential. Furthermore, **Masyn Winn** (50.22) is facing the formidable Imanaga, and with SB being our scarcest category, his efficiency remains under the microscope; we are sacrificing a bit of raw projection to keep him active, hoping his speed contributes to our totals despite the tough pitching matchup. Ensure all lineup configurations are locked before first pitch, especially given the volatility associated with our bench-depth players like **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, and **Drew Gilbert**.",
